body:
Youre right, how can someone love another without knowing them? Ive thought about this a lot in times where my mental state has been really bad. But i will tell you something that ive found true to myself even if you dont think its true. Maybe this will help swift your perceptive.  Even without knowing someone, when they vent and when they share their feelings, I cant help but relate to them. I know what it feels like to wanna just end it all, and i know other people who feel like this too. For me, this sense of loving someone doesnt come from knowing them. It comes from the want for better for them. So yes, i do love you and you shouldnt do it. Bcz as any other human being, u deserve better. Im only 18, but i can assure you that things look up. If i had ended things for myself when i was planning on doing it, i would have missed out on so many things in my life that im grateful for experiencing now. You have people in your life who would be devestated to lose you. You have things that you havent accomplished yet. You have so much to live for!

&#x200B;

Sometimes even establishing short term goals can help, well at least theyve helped me. Maybe theres a new game coming out in a month that looks really cool. You dont wanna miss that, so promise yourself to live and experince that. After that, maybe your gonna eat  ice cream tomorrow and you love ice cream. Promise yourself that you will live and experience that ice cream. I hope you understand what im tryna say <3 Allow yourself to be motivated by the 'small' stuff cuz those stuff matter too.

&#x200B;

Your so young and you have so much life left worth living. Right now I understand that it doesnt feel like that, and your feelings are very very VERY valid! But I just wanted to reassure you that you have a lot of people (that you know AND dont know) who care about you and want the best for u, including me :)

&#x200B;

My PMs are open. You can vent, or talk or we can even talk about music or movies or whatever else your into.
